# Incident on 2026-11-25 - Outage due to Modsec Rules Put In To Block GOV.UK Prototype RCE Vulnerability

## Key events
  - Disruption started 2026-11-25 17:03
  - Disruption detected 2026-11-25 17:03
  - Cloud Platform team announced that they were rolling back the ingress changes 2026-11-25 17:11
  - Rollback completed 2026-11-25 17:29
  - Fixed version applied to non-production 2026-11-25 18:19
  - Fixed version applied to production 2026-11-25 18:49

## Identified
  Via user reports and Cloud Platform engineer investigation of ingress controller logs.

## Background
  A Remote Code Execution (RCE) vulnerability was identified affecting the GOV.UK Prototype Kit, which is used by multiple teams to develop and host application prototypes.

  The vulnerability was reported through [Wiz finding (wct-id-3959)](https://app.wiz.io/issues?filters={%22risk%22%3A{%22includesAny%22%3A[%22wct-id-3959%22]}}) and the CP team created [issue 187 in the CP backlog](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/cloud-platform-security-issues/issues/187).

  Two potential mitigations were identified and the CP team worked on implementing them:

  1. Block `/plugin-assets/govuk-prototype-kit` at the ingress level.
  2. Apply a global ModSecurity rule for services using the ModSecurity ingress controllers.

  Both mitigations were initially implemented in [PR 195 - Block Manage Prototype](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/cloud-platform-terraform-ingress-controller/pull/195). The rollout of the mitigation subsequently caused an outage.
  
  A corrected configuration was later implemented in [PR 196 - Fix ModSecurity rule for GOV.UK Prototype Kit](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/cloud-platform-terraform-ingress-controller/pull/196)

## Impact
  Services using affected ModSecurity ingress controllers experienced disruption following deployment of the mitigation. Development teams reported certificate warnings and users were unable to access affected services. The issue was caused by ingress controller configuration failures resulting from a duplicate ModSecurity rule ID. Because of this, the modsec ingress controller configuration was not successfully loaded resulting in the disruption to services.  Only services using the modsec ingress controller were impacted, other serivces continued to be accessible.

  There is no evidence that the GOV.UK Prototype Kit vulnerability was exploited. The outage was caused by deployment of the mitigation rather than exploitation of the vulnerability itself.

